.\" man/man3/Docv::Corpus.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Corpus" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Corpus \- The plain text of many pages, for finding text across all of them: each page laid out at \fB\%WIDTH\fR columns (wrapped, without header and footer), one line per line with text, its blanks at either end stripped.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Corpus\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The plain text of many pages, for finding text across all of them: each
page laid out at \fB\%WIDTH\fR columns (wrapped, without header and footer),
one line per line with text, its blanks at either end stripped.
.PP
The text lives in a cache file (\fB\%Corpus.cache_path\fR) that is mapped into
memory, one record per page with the page\(aqs modification time. \fB\%build\fR
takes a page\(aqs text from the cache while the time matches and parses
the other pages, then writes a new cache. Parsing allocates constantly,
and the garbage collector\(aqs allocation lock keeps threads of one process
from parsing faster together, so with a \fB\%Corpus.worker\fR command the pages
are parsed by \fIthreads\fR worker processes (\fB\%Corpus.serve\fR), otherwise one
by one in this process. \fB\%count\fR searches every page on \fIthreads\fR
searcher threads, each a fiber in an isolated execution context (a
thread of its own) that waits for searches on a channel.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
corpus = Docv::Corpus.new
corpus.build([Docv::Corpus::Source.new("/usr/share/man/man1/ls.1.gz", mtime)])
corpus.count("sort time") # => [3]
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBCHUNK = 64\fR
Pages a search fiber takes at a time.
.PP
\fBFILE = "text.bin"\fR
.TP 4
\fBHEADER = "docv text 1"\fR
First line of the cache file; another value discards the file.
.TP 4
\fBPAGE_TIMEOUT = 30.seconds\fR
Longest wait for a worker process to send one page.
.TP 4
\fBWIDTH = 80\fR
Columns the pages are laid out at.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(cache : String = Corpus.cache_path, threads : Int32 = 0)\fR
A corpus cached in \fIcache\fR, working on \fIthreads\fR processes and fibers
(0: one less than the processor count).
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.cache_path : String\fR
The default cache file: \fB\%$XDG_CACHE_HOME/docv/text.bin\fR, or
\fB\%\(ti/.cache/docv/text.bin\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.extract(path : String) : String\fR
The text of the page at \fIpath\fR: its lines at \fB\%WIDTH\fR columns with text,
stripped, each ending in a newline. Empty when the page cannot be read.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.serve(input : IO = STDIN, output : IO = STDOUT) : Nil\fR
Runs a worker process: reads page paths from \fIinput\fR, one per line,
and writes the size of each page\(aqs text (\fB\%extract\fR) on a line of its
own, then the text, to \fIoutput\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.worker : Array(String) | Nil\fR
The command that starts a worker process, which runs \fB\%Corpus.serve\fR;
\fB\%nil\fR parses in this process. The \fB\%docv\fR command sets itself with its
\fB\%text\-worker\fR subcommand.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.worker=(worker : Array(String) | Nil)\fR
The command that starts a worker process, which runs \fB\%Corpus.serve\fR;
\fB\%nil\fR parses in this process. The \fB\%docv\fR command sets itself with its
\fB\%text\-worker\fR subcommand.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef build(sources : Array(Source), & : Int32, Int32 \-> ) : Nil\fR
Makes the text of \fIsources\fR available, in their order: from the cache
where a page\(aqs modification time matches, from parsing it otherwise,
writing a new cache when anything was parsed. Yields the pages parsed
so far and the number to parse, in the calling fiber.
.TP 4
\fBdef build(sources : Array(Source)) : Nil\fR
Builds without reporting progress.
.TP 4
\fBdef cache : String\fR
The cache file.
.TP 4
\fBdef close : Nil\fR
Unmaps the cache file and stops the searchers.
.TP 4
\fBdef count(query : String, cancelled : Proc(Bool) = \-> do
  false
end) : Array(Int32) | Nil\fR
Counts, per page, the lines that every space\-separated term of \fIquery\fR
matches (\fB\%Fuzzy#match?\fR), searching on \fB\%threads\fR threads in parallel.
Returns \fB\%nil\fR when the query has no terms, the corpus is not built, or
\fIcancelled\fR turned true meanwhile (it is called from those threads).
.TP 4
\fBdef ready? : Bool\fR
True once \fB\%build\fR finished.
.TP 4
\fBdef text(index : Int32) : Bytes\fR
The text of page \fIindex\fR: lines ending in newlines; empty when the
page has none or the corpus is not built.
.TP 4
\fBdef threads : Int32\fR
Worker processes that parse, and fibers that search, in parallel.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/corpus.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Corpus::Source" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Fuzzy" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
